# Pairs with GuardCoversFence. The post-failure resync marks the instance's
# view of TAIL current but re-seeds from its own allocator and the calls in
# motion, not from the TAIL it read: after a stale commit is refused because a
# predecessor on another silo moved TAIL, the instance claims offsets at or
# below the committed tail it has just observed.
MODULE: GuardCoversFenceResyncKeepsStaleGuard
TARGET: GuardCoversFence
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the resync refreshes the fence but keeps its stale guard below the observed TAIL
PERTURBS: Resync

--- FIND
    /\ inflight = {}
    /\ next' = ReseedNext
--- REPLACE
    /\ inflight = {}
\* MUTATION: the re-seed ignores the TAIL it read.
    /\ next' = Max({next} \cup {o + 1 : o \in orphans \ hidden})
--- END
--- FIND
WithCrossSiloMove == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: raises the bound so a lost activation may move to another silo.
WithCrossSiloMove == TRUE
--- END
